{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes","id":1480407,"title":"The difference between Werewolf and Vampire's themes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-07T14:05:09-07:00","id":1480407,"title":"The difference between Werewolf and Vampire's themes","content":"I wrote this over in the Tzimisce thread and thought it was relevant. Basically, my idea about the different themes of the games and what they emphasize.<br /> <br /> I was curious how you saw the difference between the two games and what gets to the heart of them.<br /> <br /> <b>The difference between V:TM and W:TA</b><br /> <br /> Well focusing on that, I suppose it's not just what VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE is but also what WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE is. I've mentioned that V:TM is Gothic Punk horror fiction about sin, damnation, and remorse from your activities. It is about coping with a dreadful curse and dealing with the fact that you are now divorced from whoever you are while alive. Also, the fact that you are immortal and trapped in a feudalist exploitative super-capitalist society where the rich are literal predators on the poor.<br /> <br /> W:TA by contrast is Tragic Heroic Mythology. Whereas vampire is Jane Eye, Wuthering Heights, and The Anarchist's Cookbook, W:TA is Beowulf, Oedipus Rex, and Last of the Mohicans. Werewolves have a lot of curse-like elements but their actual curse is the fact that they are going to lose Ragnarok and die fighting the Dragon and realize they've married their mother.<br /> <br /> Werewolves don't have the kind of self-loathing narcissistic tragedy that vampires do and, generally, all love being werewolves (I'm simplifying). They, however, are destined to throw themselves into the jaws of death to try to save the world. In V:TM, you are the monster. In Werewolf, you are not THE monster but slay the monster. It's just THE monster is going to win.<br /> <br /> And like all great heroes like Sigurd or Gilgamesh, they're horribly flawed in some way that is going to make their loss inevitable too.<br /> <br /> (Why I actually think Lunars/Werewolves fit into Exalted just fine)<br /> <br /> Souleaters don't work for V:TM because, while there's nothing wrong with it, <i>Angel: The Series</i> is not how you're meant to run being undead. Generally, most vampires are not heroes and fighting evil. A single vampire or coterie of vampires fighting evil is fine, I've run many a game like that but they're an aberration. Most vampires do not give a shit and if they found out there was a corporation making a deal with Satan to make more money, 50% of all vampires would react with, &quot;Okay, THAT is a hot stock tip. Where do I invest in this Pentex?&quot; Another 25% will go, &quot;Okay, not my problem.&quot; Another 10% will be like, &quot;Ah ha! A rival!&quot; With maybe 5% appropriately horrified.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: The Apocalypse, by contrast, is a game where you need an assortment of monsters and horrifying cannon fodder because they are defined by throwing themselves into the jaws of Fenris. It doesn't matter that Formori are victims of the Wyrm, they're people to be killed because a werewolf lives for violence and dies by violence.<br /> <br /> At least that's my view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T16:11:08-07:00","id":1480422,"title":"","content":"To me, there is also the difference in themes of living and seeing the world between them.<br /> <br /> In Vampire, your goal is to survive. Night in and night out, you do your best to see another moonrise. Everything you do is to ensure you may survive and be in favour of the group of vampires you hang out with and the vampire society you follow. You might be interested in the mythology of Cain, but you might as well not be.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf, your goal is to see the world survive. Inch by inch, you fight to fix what was broken no matter how desperate. You have a pack, your pack is your closest family. Your focus in growing your power is not to survive, but to fight the foe better. You often live more in the mythology of your species than in the modern world, depending on the tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T16:56:34-07:00","id":1480427,"title":"","content":"I tend to define the &quot;big three&quot; games (Vampire, Werewolf, Mage) as being games of Personal Horror, Savage Horror, and Gnostic Horror, respectively. Unfortunately I'm running on fumes at the moment and too tired to fully describe what I mean by that. Hopefully I can expand on it tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T23:19:54-07:00","id":1480452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes#post1480407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A single vampire or coterie of vampires fighting evil is fine, I've run many a game like that but they're an aberration. Most vampires do not give a shit and if they found out there was a corporation making a deal with Satan to make more money, 50% of all vampires would react with, &quot;Okay, THAT is a hot stock tip. Where do I invest in this Pentex?&quot; Another 25% will go, &quot;Okay, not my problem.&quot; Another 10% will be like, &quot;Ah ha! A rival!&quot; With maybe 5% appropriately horrified.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My good sir, i must say your interpretation is outrageously incorrect and misguided on many levels.<br /> <br /> 50% of all vampires would react with, &quot;Okay, THAT is a hot mess to distract the hunters with, time for anonymous tip.&quot; Another 25% will go, &quot;Okay, what local kindred are <i>in need of something</i> to get hunters out of their trails? Time to collect some major favors.&quot; While another 10% will be like, &quot;how much can hunter intervention plummet their stocks in the market - and should i cash in while they are down? Decisions, decisions...&quot; With maybe 5% appropriately horrified they didn't think of doing <b><i>all of the above</i></b>, since these are not on themselves mutually exclusive options.<br /> <br /> Honestly, pardon my bluntness but i felt it extremely necessary to correct you and get the facts right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T17:53:09-07:00","id":1480497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480452#post1480452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My good sir, i must say your interpretation is outrageously incorrect and misguided on many levels.<br /> <br /> 50% of all vampires would react with, &quot;Okay, THAT is a hot mess to distract the hunters with, time for anonymous tip.&quot; Another 25% will go, &quot;Okay, what local kindred are <i>in need of something</i> to get hunters out of their trails? Time to collect some major favors.&quot; While another 10% will be like, &quot;how much can hunter intervention plummet their stocks in the market - and should i cash in while they are down? Decisions, decisions...&quot; With maybe 5% appropriately horrified they didn't think of doing <b><i>all of the above</i></b>, since these are not on themselves mutually exclusive options.<br /> <br /> Honestly, pardon my bluntness but i felt it extremely necessary to correct you and get the facts right.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you just want to distract hunters, you go for something more innocuous than a multinational that can make scary monsters out of normal kine. If the hunters get riled up and attack... they will probably die horribly, and some of them might remember that they had a mysterious tip get them into this while writhing around in a vat while they get turned into one of said monsters. Standard vampire methods for social maneuvers need some tweaking at the very least to go up against the Even Edgier Chronos Corporation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T23:01:19-07:00","id":1480513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes#post1480407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well focusing on that, I suppose it's not just what VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE is but also what WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE is. I've mentioned that V:TM is Gothic Punk horror fiction about sin, damnation, and remorse from your activities. It is about coping with a dreadful curse and dealing with the fact that you are now divorced from whoever you are while alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two ways to look at this. The first is that difference in intended themes by the developers of the game. &quot;Personal Horror&quot; versus &quot;Savage Horror&quot;. whatever that might mean. Then there are the implicit differences from embedded pop culture themes between the two kinds of monsters.<br /> <br /> For example, Vampire's game mechanics makes Humanity important. Werewolf has no such mechanics. So as designed, Werewolf is much less about &quot;personal horror.&quot; But the game designers intended Werewolf to be about giving a damn about the world around you (when will you Rage), so the setting (in terms of the Litany and antagonists) is designed to bring that about.<br /> <br /> In contrast, there are certain implicit themes. Many werewolf movies and books have an implied personal horror theme, even more than vampire. Because vampires, despite needing to live by feeding off the blood of humans, generally aren't presented as caring about that. But since 1941's Wolfman, werewolves are often depicted as not wanting to do the things they are compelled to do. Personal horror should be part of the genre. But W:tA's setting and mechanics generally play it down. It only happens if a PC or ST really push it in roleplay. On the other hand, cinematic werewolves are often depicted as being in opposition to other monsters, because the &quot;thinking&quot; side of the monster - the human who doesn't want to kill - sympathizes with the victims of the monsters. So the Wolf Man fights Frankenstein's Monster, Dracula, and other monsters. So WtA having fomori pretty much emulates the same thing.<br /> <br /> And there are plenty of other implicit themes. If you explore the Wolf Man, Howling, American Werewolf in London, Wolfen, Werewolf of Paris, Wolf, and many other werewolf media, legend, and folklore, there are lots of other themes. We've gotten into some of them in the other thread talking about the movie Howling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes#post1480407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the fact that you are immortal and trapped in a feudalist exploitative super-capitalist society where the rich are literal predators on the poor.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only comment on this is you are wrong about limiting it to capitalism. Humanity is a hierarchical species. We see the same behavior in humans as we see in chimpanzees. Capitalism has nothing to do with it. It's why explicitly anti-capitalist societies like communism, various non-communist socialist societies, and pre-capitalist societies are just as exploitative if not more. There will always be an elite. And there will always be a need for somebody to shovel shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes#post1480407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W:TA by contrast is Tragic Heroic Mythology. Whereas vampire is Jane Eye, Wuthering Heights, and The Anarchist's Cookbook, W:TA is Beowulf, Oedipus Rex, and Last of the Mohicans. Werewolves have a lot of curse-like elements but their actual curse is the fact that they are going to lose Ragnarok and die fighting the Dragon and realize they've married their mother.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely the culture of the Garou. They are an aristocratic warrior culture. However, the setting does not define what the PCs will do. Just as vampire PCs won't necessarily act as appropriate in the feudal culture that defines vampire society, PCs won't necessarily act appropriately as in the Iliad.<br /> <br /> However, Werewolf has Renown which is a very different mechanic than Status. Status doesn't drive anything. As a marker of reputation, even Anarchs could have Status of a kind. Renown, though, drives things to a much greater extent because Renown means Rank, and Rank drives what Gifts one could learn. And while it is always possible for even Ronin to learn Gifts, in practice it's much more of an obstacle. Thus the mechanics push PCs to uphold standard Garou culture in a way that Vampire does not push Caitiff and Anarchs to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes#post1480407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves don't have the kind of self-loathing narcissistic tragedy that vampires do and, generally, all love being werewolves (I'm simplifying). They, however, are destined to throw themselves into the jaws of death to try to save the world. In V:TM, you are the monster. In Werewolf, you are not THE monster but slay the monster. It's just THE monster is going to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>This really depends on the ST because there are at least concepts in the setting which delve into the same categories. Werewolves have Lunatics, Harano, and the Curse. An ST who wants to highlight those can create elements which come close to the same things in Vampire. And many STs in Vampire don't play particular attention to Humanity and personal horror because they get in the way of sect wars or other combat activity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes#post1480407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf: The Apocalypse, by contrast, is a game where you need an assortment of monsters and horrifying cannon fodder because they are defined by throwing themselves into the jaws of Fenris. It doesn't matter that Formori are victims of the Wyrm, they're people to be killed because a werewolf lives for violence and dies by violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf as a game has outside antagonists. You are monsters fighting other monsters. So yeah, PCs kill them. The Vampire setting generally ignores other creatures. It's very insular. You only deal with other vampires and humans because the game's sourcebooks never really address other creatures as potential antagonists. If they did, then vampires would probably treat them just as well as werewolves do - you kill them because they don't matter. Because Vampire was the first WoD game, it had to be insular. There weren't other games to reference. While each later game had to reference the games before it to some degree. But there isn't anything stopping a Vampire ST from including certain creatures/splats if they wanted. If they don't, it's more because of inertia (because the sourcebooks tend not to include them) as opposed to them somehow being intriniscally incorrect to do so.<br /> <br /> But werewolf definitely designed fomori to avoid mortal entanglements. Once someone becomes fomori, it's pretty much unredeemable. You can't &quot;un-fomori&quot; or &quot;de-fomori&quot; them as written. There's no myth like Golconda because things are written from the perspective of the Garou. Garou probably ignore any evidence that there is something like Golconda for vampires too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T17:54:31-07:00","id":1480605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480513#post1480513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But werewolf definitely designed fomori to avoid mortal entanglements. Once someone becomes fomori, it's pretty much unredeemable. You can't &quot;un-fomori&quot; or &quot;de-fomori&quot; them as written. There's no myth like Golconda because things are written from the perspective of the Garou. Garou probably ignore any evidence that there is something like Golconda for vampires too.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally possibly as written, in the text of the Possession Charm. It takes kicking out the bane via Exorcism or similar effects and healing 10 levels of creeping, unsoakable agg that ticks by afterward (probably by using Mother's Touch at a vital threshold of timing), however, so it's not something that they can do without risk of consequences (not even Gurahl can, per their rite for the same end). As for Golconda, where's the evidence that's supposed to sway the Garou to believing it's possible? Aren't licks that achieve it supposed to be so vanishingly rare that you'll likely never meet them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T18:00:40-07:00","id":1480606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480605#post1480605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's literally possibly as written, in the text of the Possession Charm. It takes kicking out the bane via Exorcism or similar effects and healing 10 levels of creeping, unsoakable agg that ticks by afterward (probably by using Mother's Touch at a vital threshold of timing), however, so it's not something that they can do without risk of consequences (not even Gurahl can, per their rite for the same end). As for Golconda, where's the evidence that's supposed to sway the Garou to believing it's possible? Aren't licks that achieve it supposed to be so vanishingly rare that you'll likely never meet them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves aren't really too concerned about collateral damage anyway. Redeemable vampires doesn't really seem like it would really factor into their moral calculus anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T20:11:25-07:00","id":1480719,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think most vampires even know what Golconda is, and if they ran into a vampire they'd probably just kill it. That said, presumaqbly vampires in Golconda don't trigger Sense Wyrm, so it's possible that werewolves wouldn't even notice the vampire around in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T21:56:51-07:00","id":1480727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480719#post1480719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't think most vampires even know what Golconda is, and if they ran into a vampire they'd probably just kill it. That said, presumaqbly vampires in Golconda don't trigger Sense Wyrm, so it's possible that werewolves wouldn't even notice the vampire around in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>As written, any vampire who has a Humanity of 7 or greater doesn't register with Sense Wyrm, and I believe Gangrel don't detect even at lower Humanity (I want to say not until Humanity 4, but I can't remember what book states this) and there can be special merits which prevent it at all. So vampires who have achieved Golconda must by definition be Humanity 10 and won't detect as Wyrm.<br /> <br /> This is one of the big reasons why 1e WoD was open to some interaction between vampires and werewolves. Certainly many Garou wouldn't care at all - if the encounter any vampire they will destroy them regardless of whether Sense Wyrm goes off. But certainly the Children of Gaia and some others might be more tender hearted. And the Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers tend to make pragmatic decisions with the local vampires so that it is not constant warfare. And some camps are into working with one group of Wyrm minions to turn them against other Wyrm minions, or just to exploit them for their own purposes.<br /> <br /> So while I've noticed many players refusing to tolerate any relations between Garou and werewolves, early WoD made an effort to show it could happen. If anything, the multiple instances in 1e that showed vampires and Garou getting along bothered enough players to stage a counter reaction. While it was always supposed to be an exception, many players thought it happened way too much. So the fanbase started reacting by saying it would never happen. Personally, I do think it's OK in the setting to allow there not to be total warfare all the time. But every ST and player group will have a different tolerance level as to when it happens too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T14:21:37-07:00","id":1480763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480727#post1480727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As written, any vampire who has a Humanity of 7 or greater doesn't register with Sense Wyrm, and I believe Gangrel don't detect even at lower Humanity (I want to say not until Humanity 4, but I can't remember what book states this) and there can be special merits which prevent it at all. So vampires who have achieved Golconda must by definition be Humanity 10 and won't detect as Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gangrel don't get a pass on that mechanic, as far as W:tA is concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is one of the big reasons why 1e WoD was open to some interaction between vampires and werewolves. Certainly many Garou wouldn't care at all - if the encounter any vampire they will destroy them regardless of whether Sense Wyrm goes off. But certainly the Children of Gaia and some others might be more tender hearted. And the Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers tend to make pragmatic decisions with the local vampires so that it is not constant warfare. And some camps are into working with one group of Wyrm minions to turn them against other Wyrm minions, or just to exploit them for their own purposes.<br /> <br /> So while I've noticed many players refusing to tolerate any relations between Garou and werewolves, early WoD made an effort to show it could happen. If anything, the multiple instances in 1e that showed vampires and Garou getting along bothered enough players to stage a counter reaction. While it was always supposed to be an exception, many players thought it happened way too much. So the fanbase started reacting by saying it would never happen. Personally, I do think it's OK in the setting to allow there not to be total warfare all the time. But every ST and player group will have a different tolerance level as to when it happens too much. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about that. I learned W:tA on a 1e core and it... didn't seem very concerned about supporting crossover friends. This really goes back to the werewolf in Hunter's Hunted, who was out to kill vampires, albeit because of a women in refrigerators vengeance reason. Also, a number of tribes (&quot;more tender-hearted&quot; CoGs, for example) have alliances with sun-related spirits, which I can't imagine being conducive to alliances or even casual interaction with vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T20:34:20-07:00","id":1480795,"title":"","content":"The difference is that werewolf is a superhero game, and vampire isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T02:13:57-07:00","id":1480817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480795#post1480795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is that werewolf is a superhero game, and vampire isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I state the Lunars never need to be updated since the Garou fit into that setting just fine as is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T06:22:40-07:00","id":1480825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480795#post1480795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is that werewolf is a superhero game, and vampire isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just my personal opinion, but it won't be very superhero if you also take in the WOLF part of the WERE. I personally dislike the mostly human focused way of playing WtA, because it truly does feel like superheroes and not feral beasts.<br /> <br /> This is why I always try to put focus on the animal and spirit sides over the human. This might be because I came to WtA not from other tabletop games, but from Wolf RPs. So my focus is different XD<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T07:21:06-07:00","id":1480829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480825#post1480825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is just my personal opinion, but it won't be very superhero if you also take in the WOLF part of the WERE. I personally dislike the mostly human focused way of playing WtA, because it truly does feel like superheroes and not feral beasts.<br /> <br /> This is why I always try to put focus on the animal and spirit sides over the human. This might be because I came to WtA not from other tabletop games, but from Wolf RPs. So my focus is different XD</div> </div> </div> </div>It would still be a game where your superpowers increase because you were consistently courageous, wise, and honorable. And it would still be a game where you run around with magic swords wearing clothes in crinos form. You are, therefore, still going to be pushed towards being a Lawful-Good Druid/Barbarian multi-class who eventually adds levels in Rogue, Wizard, Paladin, Bard, or Fighter. With a werewolf paint-job.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T10:12:37-07:00","id":1480843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480829#post1480829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would still be a game where your superpowers increase because you were consistently courageous, wise, and honorable. And it would still be a game where you run around with magic swords wearing clothes in crinos form. You are, therefore, still going to be pushed towards being a Lawful-Good Druid/Barbarian multi-class who eventually adds levels in Rogue, Wizard, Paladin, Bard, or Fighter. With a werewolf paint-job.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you feel so strongly about that, could you please lay out your ideal type of werewolf here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1479701-other-werewolf-option\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...erewolf-option</a><br /> <br /> I am not joking, I want to hear from people like you WHAT would you like to play instead of the garou?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T10:24:40-07:00","id":1480844,"title":"","content":"I don't feel strongly about that. I'm simply stating an observation, not a preference, not a criticism. Werewolf the Apocalypse is a superhero game about Druid/Barbarian multiclassers strongly mechanically motivated to be courageous, wise, and honorable. Whether that is a good or bad thing is up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T11:48:31-07:00","id":1480847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480844#post1480844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel strongly about that. I'm simply stating an observation, not a preference, not a criticism. Werewolf the Apocalypse is a superhero game about Druid/Barbarian multiclassers strongly mechanically motivated to be courageous, wise, and honorable. Whether that is a good or bad thing is up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing; The game should -not- be a superhero story. It is a game of Savage Horror. So if you see it as a superhero story, something about the setting is not working correctly for you. And I'm interested to know -what- it is and how would you change the game to make it fit a Savage Horror label better?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T12:48:38-07:00","id":1480852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480844#post1480844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel strongly about that. I'm simply stating an observation, not a preference, not a criticism. Werewolf the Apocalypse is a superhero game about Druid/Barbarian multiclassers strongly mechanically motivated to be courageous, wise, and honorable. Whether that is a good or bad thing is up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Superhero&quot; was an approach that was listed in the 1e core for chronicle ideas. It hasn't really made a return since, and for good reason - the day to day life of werewolves typically means someone ends up dead. So they can't be hall monitors like Colossus; at their most benevolent, they are Deadpool, but without the fourth wall breaks. And if they've gotten too close to the Wyld under the mistaken assumption that it is their friend because it hates the Weaver and Wyrm forces that are encroaching on the werewolf's home, they might actually retain the fourth wall breaks, as well as the appearance of an avocado that fucked an older, uglier avocado. The Wyrm isn't the only flame that it's dangerous to dance around.<br /> <br /> Also, to stringently and over-literally correct your D&amp;D analogy, druids and barbarians didn't get anything like what Garou have until 3e to 4e, and that's gone as of 5e. Worth noting also that there was a berserker class in the Viking &quot;historical&quot; campaign sourcebook for 2e that gave a slightly freer hand with shapeshifting, but when you can just decide to fluidly change shape at a moment's notice with mechanical effect, D&amp;D blows a gasket, because you have short-circuited every &quot;neat trick&quot; DMs have to keep treasure away from you on the other side of the puzzle, which apparently needs to be the balancing factor for everything in the dragon game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T12:57:38-07:00","id":1480854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480847#post1480847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the thing; The game should -not- be a superhero story. It is a game of Savage Horror. So if you see it as a superhero story, something about the setting is not working correctly for you. And I'm interested to know -what- it is and how would you change the game to make it fit a Savage Horror label better?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know that I could change it to make it a game of savage horror. Being a game about Druid/Barbarian multiclassed superheroes is so deep in it's DNA that you'd pretty much need to start from scratch and make a whole new game that had nothing in common with this one but the name. This isn't something that could be changed with just a couple of minor tweeks. You'd need to completely dump the renown system and make progression based off something horrific. You'd need to almost completely dump the spirit world so the werewolves don't have a place of beauty and wonder to escape to. You'd need to make frenzy a much bigger problem.<br /> <br /> Understand that I'm not recommending any of that. I'm quite neutral on it. I'm simply saying that's the sort of thing it would take to make this a game of savage horror. If you like the things I've said would need to be purged to make this a game of savage horror, that's fine. But just understand that you are liking a superhero game. Which is also fine. I've played unrepentant superhero games and quite enjoyed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T17:27:37-07:00","id":1480901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480854#post1480854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know that I could change it to make it a game of savage horror. Being a game about Druid/Barbarian multiclassed superheroes is so deep in it's DNA that you'd pretty much need to start from scratch and make a whole new game that had nothing in common with this one but the name. This isn't something that could be changed with just a couple of minor tweeks. You'd need to completely dump the renown system and make progression based off something horrific.</div> </div> </div> </div>The implications of Renown as-is are a big part of why they've hoisted themselves with their own petard, as well as quite horrific when one stops to consider that Honor requires upholding the Veil, i.e. disappearing people who know who and what they really are. You can't speak up against your ancestors without compromising your place in Garou society. You can't go against elders without taking a risk that you'll compromise your place in it and also end up challenged to a fight to the death. Honor for monsters is scary, above and beyond that they have to rack up a huge body count for Glory and do unreliable and suspect things to advance Wisdom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'd need to almost completely dump the spirit world so the werewolves don't have a place of beauty and wonder to escape to. </div> </div> </div>You need contrast for proper horror. That's why a good portion of the Umbra is a nightmare horrorscape with spirits ranging between alien and hostile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'd need to make frenzy a much bigger problem. </div> </div> </div>Roll a good portion of it back to 1e. Thrall of the Wyrm doesn't exist as such but the uncontrollable nature of rolling too many successes to frenzy still does, along with the risk of eating what you kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T18:54:25-07:00","id":1480918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480795#post1480795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is that werewolf is a superhero game, and vampire isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I think you probably didn't go through the 90s vampions through &quot;space&quot; (umbra) with celerity and potence 8 games lol<br /> <br /> Any WoD game is what the ST and his group wants it to be. You can emphasize some themes or not. Werewolf is a tragedy, just as much as vampire (or mage) has the potential to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T22:30:15-07:00","id":1480929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480854#post1480854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Understand that I'm not recommending any of that. I'm quite neutral on it. I'm simply saying that's the sort of thing it would take to make this a game of savage horror. If you like the things I've said would need to be purged to make this a game of savage horror, that's fine. But just understand that you are liking a superhero game. Which is also fine. I've played unrepentant superhero games and quite enjoyed them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understand that even if you do not intend it, calling WtA a superhero game is still implying that the game is not delivering on its savage horror side for you.<br /> <br /> I might like the superhero game, but I'm also trying to understand the reasons why people do not and what things are the sticking point.<br /> <br /> So I thank you for giving your opinions on it, I'll take note of those aspects.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T01:06:25-07:00","id":1480946,"title":"","content":"In the end, it comes to the individual ST how much savage horror is in the game.<br /> Personally, I can't really deliver gory, violent, scenes or savage beasts and the combat system doesn't help. If I describe something there is always an urge by amongst the players to roll for something. It's this agency over characters thing.<br /> So, I'm mostly stuck to describe situations the PC approach, like &quot;crime scene&quot;-descriptions and the players have to use a bit of their own imagination to visualize it. Thing is, modern media have a bit over saturated this element, so there isn't that much to shock, unless one involves NPCs the characters hold dear or the PCs themselves in some way.<br /> <br /> Taking over the PC, for example when in a frenzy, might do the trick, but also has it's limits and also builds up a barrier between the player and the characters deeds.<br /> <br /> So, the trick is, to find ways to gently force the players into having their characters perform savage deeds themselves and later be afraid of what they did...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T06:59:42-07:00","id":1480961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480829#post1480829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would still be a game where your superpowers increase because you were consistently courageous, wise, and honorable. And it would still be a game where you run around with magic swords wearing clothes in crinos form. You are, therefore, still going to be pushed towards being a Lawful-Good Druid/Barbarian multi-class who eventually adds levels in Rogue, Wizard, Paladin, Bard, or Fighter. With a werewolf paint-job.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that depends on how you view Garou society because I'd argue that Garou values tend toward more Lawful Evil than Lawful Good.<br /> <br /> Which is what some people are trying to fix.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T17:58:38-07:00","id":1481153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480407-the-difference-between-werewolf-and-vampire-s-themes?p=1480946#post1480946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, modern media have a bit over saturated this element, so there isn't that much to shock, unless one involves NPCs the characters hold dear or the PCs themselves in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a sticking point with WOD in general.<br /> <br /> In IRL modern nights, people have had Gore Story, Slap-fight 4: the revengeance on-demand for over a decade now to desensitize them. The most &quot;shocking&quot; things WOD can pull are going to be a bit quaint at best.<br /> <br /> This also impacts the kinds of in-depth character dramas that WOD wants to tell, because there's an oversaturated market of stories that tackle all the &quot;big&quot; topics like War, PTSD, Rape, Oppression, Corrupt government and Civilian systems, Artificial divides by sex/race/culture/country/etc..., because the shear amount of authors using those topics to try and stand out. Anyone looking for a gripping war drama centered around the spiritual corruption and madness that results from conflict can pick up a copy of &quot;Spec Ops: The Line&quot; and have a story written by professional writers at the top of their game as opposed to what their ST could come up with for that campaign.<br /> <br /> This is kinda why I oppose the idea that the games need to stay &quot;on theme&quot;. The game's themes aren't unique enough to be worth putting them in a box that makes them one-note and unable to grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}